>>
endobj
901 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 215 0 R
/E (Primary Issue : creation of a Designated Authority  to supervise, manage, and dispose of the foreign contribution and any assets created from it, whenever an organisation's FCRA registration is cancelled, surrendered, or otherwise ceases)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [19]
>>
endobj
902 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 215 0 R
/T (Way Forward on FCRA)
/E (Way Forward on FCRA)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [20]
>>
endobj
903 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1829 0 R
/E (Statutory definitions for contested terms: Define 'proselytisation', 'political nature' and other discretion-conferring terms in the Act/Rules itself \(rather than leaving them to administrative interpretation\), incorporating the Supreme Court's INSAF \(2020\) narrowing.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [21]
>>
endobj
904 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1830 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [22]
>>
endobj
905 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1831 0 R
/E (Time-bound, reasoned suspension/cancellation orders: Statutorily mandate reasoned, time-bound orders with a structured appellate mechanism, reducing reliance on writ litigation as the only recourse.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [23]
>>
endobj
906 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1832 0 R
/E (Proportionate treatment of the Designated Authority's asset powers: Given the disposal/permanent-transfer power in the pending Bill, build in judicial or quasi-judicial oversight before assets are permanently disposed of, and a realistic, extendable window for organisations to secure fresh registration before assets are treated as permanently vested.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [24]
>>
endobj
907 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1833 0 R
/E (Parliamentary scrutiny: Refer significant future amendments to a Standing/Joint Parliamentary Committee, given the scale, cumulative impact, and stakeholder concern already evident around the 2026 Bill, to build broader legislative consensus and consultation.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [25]
>>
endobj
908 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1834 0 R
/E (Simplify compliance for low-risk NGOs: Introduce a lighter-touch, lower-fee compliance track for small NGOs with modest, single-purpose foreign funding, reserving intensive purpose/geography-specific scrutiny for higher-value or sensitive-sector recipients.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [26]
>>
endobj
909 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1835 0 R
/E (Publish aggregate compliance data regularly: Institutionalise periodic public reporting \(beyond ad hoc Parliament questions\) on FCRA registrations, cancellations, penalties and utilisation patterns to build public trust and enable independent research and accountability.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [27]
>>
endobj
910 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1836 0 R
/E (Dialogue with faith-based and minority-serving organisations: Given specific apprehensions raised by the Catholic Bishops' Conference of India and the Kerala Assembly, structured pre-legislative consultation with affected religious/minority-welfare organisations would improve both legitimacy and drafting precision of contested provisions.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [28]
>>
endobj
